name: Browse complete accepted groups and individual observations
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/groups.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: groups
require-live-snap: 30 2 groups / 65 findings | complete-groups
ask: Does Review distinguish two presentation groups from sixty-five independent findings without claiming decisions or full coverage?
require-live-snap: 20 GROUPS · Enter members | group-navigation
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 GROUP MEMBERS | first-members
keys: n
require-live-snap: 25 Rows 51-64 / 64 | last-members
keys: j j j j j j j j j j j j j
require-live-snap: 20 GROUP MEMBERS · F-0065 | final-observation
keys: k k k k k k k k k k k k k
require-live-snap: 20 GROUP MEMBERS · F-0052 | selected-observation
ask: Are all sixty-four members reachable through explicit paging with their own aliases and no lost or rewritten observations?
resize: 40x12
live-snap: narrow-members
keys: PageDown
live-snap: narrow-member-detail
expect: Recorded decision: needs_review
ask: At 40x12 does the selected alias remain visible while paging its independent verdict and recorded source, with open/back controls usable?
resize: 120x36
keys: Home
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 SELECTED FINDING | opened-observation
keys: G
require-live-snap: 25 Rows 51-64 / 64 | returned-members
ask: Does opening an observation and returning with G preserve the group, member page, selection and source binding?
keys: L
require-live-snap: 25 Duplicate · Accepted | member-relationship
keys: u
require-live-snap: 20 Reason (required) | unlink-note
paste-file: @ART/unlink-note.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Duplicate · Removed | unlinked
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 25 Groups unavailable | stale-group
keys: R
require-live-snap: 25 3 groups / 65 findings | split-groups
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/groups.py @TMP_TARGET @ART removed
ask: Does explicit unlink split only the grouping while retaining all observations and verdicts, and does stale grouping require an honest refresh?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: groups
require-live-snap: 25 3 groups / 65 findings | recovered-groups
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/groups.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart preserve the split groups and original findings without another inference or finding verdict?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
